#+title: Asset selection and intake record

* Art brief
Record subject, style, scale/dimensions, animation needs, platform and budgets.

* Candidate comparison
For each candidate record creator/title, direct asset page, license URL and
included license evidence, download size, formats and dependencies. Explain
selection/rejection and any commercial-use or attribution constraints.

* Chosen files
Record pack ID, source archive URL/hash and selected member paths/hashes.
List model buffer/texture/MTL sidecars and how relative paths are preserved.
Attach original license text and complete credits. Record unchanged bytes or
specific conversion tool/version/settings and changed output provenance.

* Example failure and acceptance
A barrel GLB loads its mesh but refers to Textures/colormap.png. Include the
texture at that relative path, verify both hashes, and check shading/scale in a
real scene. Replace this example with the selected asset's actual dependency case.

* Results
Record importer/verification commands, runtime load results, visual/audio checks
and remaining limitations. Do not equate a successful hash check with rendering.
